From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] OpenGL: desktop OpenGL from an SDL 2 that defaults to OpenGL ES

An SDL 2 built for EGL with OpenGL ES only (no desktop OpenGL of its own,
as for Mesa without GLX: the ODROID-GO Ultra's panfrost) starts with an
OpenGL ES profile, and an SDL 1.2 program asking for SDL_OPENGL got a
context it cannot draw with. Ask for a desktop OpenGL compatibility
context there; Mesa gives its highest compatibility version (3.1 on
panfrost). Nothing changes where SDL 2 defaults to desktop OpenGL.

Upstream: not applicable (SDK-specific SDL 2 build)
Signed-off-by: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/SDL12_compat.c
+++ b/src/SDL12_compat.c
@@ -6650,6 +6650,21 @@
            ones did (x11, windib, quartz), so we'll just offer it everywhere. */
         GetEnvironmentWindowPosition(&x, &y);
 
+        /* An SDL 2 built for EGL with OpenGL ES only (no desktop OpenGL of
+           its own, as for Mesa without GLX) starts with an OpenGL ES profile,
+           which no SDL 1.2 program can draw with: ask for desktop OpenGL,
+           Mesa gives its highest compatibility version. */
+        if (flags20 & SDL_WINDOW_OPENGL) {
+            int profile = 0;
+
+            if (SDL20_GL_GetAttribute(SDL_GL_CONTEXT_PROFILE_MASK, &profile) == 0 &&
+                profile == SDL_GL_CONTEXT_PROFILE_ES) {
+                SDL20_GL_SetAttribute(SDL_GL_CONTEXT_PROFILE_MASK, SDL_GL_CONTEXT_PROFILE_COMPATIBILITY);
+                SDL20_GL_SetAttribute(SDL_GL_CONTEXT_MAJOR_VERSION, 2);
+                SDL20_GL_SetAttribute(SDL_GL_CONTEXT_MINOR_VERSION, 1);
+            }
+        }
+
         /* If GL scaling is disabled, and a multisampled buffer is requested, do it. */
         if (!use_gl_scaling && (flags12 & SDL12_OPENGL) && OpenGLLogicalScalingSamples) {
             SDL20_GL_SetAttribute(SDL_GL_MULTISAMPLEBUFFERS, 1);
